 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 4.258,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Has this ever happened? Shuffle a deck, and look at the order."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.1,
   "dur": 8.795,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "The first card can be any of fifty-two, the next any of the rest. Multiply all those choices, and you count the orders."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 14.7,
   "dur": 8.342,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "The answer has sixty-eight digits, too big to say out loud. Each shuffle is just one pick from that huge pile."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 24.3,
   "dur": 9.402,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Now give everyone alive a deck, eight billion of us. Shuffle once a second for fourteen billion years, the age of the universe."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 36.3,
   "dur": 10.733,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Even then, you cover less than one part in a trillion trillion trillion of the orders. Your shuffle is almost certainly the first of its kind."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 50.7,
   "dur": 7.755,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "Give the planet a thousand times more shufflers, and it barely changes. The pile of orders is just too big."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 59.7,
   "dur": 8.193,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Shuffle well, and your order has almost certainly never existed before. Not certain, but a very safe bet."
